# Keeping the build context small matters twice over: it is uploaded to the
# builder on every build, and anything copied in becomes a cache-busting input.

.git
.gitignore

# Never let a local .env reach an image layer. Even a later deletion would
# leave it recoverable in the layer history.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Rebuilt inside the image; copying host copies would both bloat the context
# and risk platform-mismatched native modules.
**/node_modules
**/.venv
**/dist

**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.ruff_cache
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache

**/*.sqlite3
**/staticfiles

# Not needed at runtime.
docs
CLAUDE.md
README.md
.github

**/.DS_Store
**/*.log
**/.vscode
**/.idea
